# DTF tier manifest: oci-digest-scope-and-promotion
#   artifact-keeper#4466, #4525, #4450, #4449 (delete by digest is scoped to
#   the image name, by-digest pulls resolve under the name, the delete
#   survives a restart, last-tag delete drops the manifest record),
#   #4568 (anonymous manifest PUT with a declared but unsent body is a 401
#   challenge, not a 500), #4558 / #4020 (/v2/token has its own bucket; wrong
#   passwords are still bounded), #4578 (a promoted Docker image is pullable
#   from the target). All 1.11.0. Profile-set: filesystem / single.
#
# THE BUGS (1.10.0 baseline)
# * #4466: `DELETE /v2/<repo>/xa/manifests/<digest>` removed the digest's tags
#   under EVERY image name in the repository, so `xb:v1` (same manifest bytes)
#   vanished with `xa`.
# * #4525: `GET/HEAD /v2/<repo>/xa/manifests/<digest>` resolved the digest
#   repository-wide, so a digest deleted under `xa` kept answering under `xa`
#   while `xb` tagged it.
# * #4450: the delete soft-deleted only the `artifacts` row at the digest path;
#   the tag's own row stayed live and the startup OCI reindex re-registered
#   the tag on the next restart: a deleted (for example compromised) image was
#   pullable again after any rollout.
# * #4449: deleting the last tag of a tag-only image left its `oci_manifests`
#   record (#4441) behind. The table does not exist on 1.10.0; the case is
#   red there by absence and asserts the row content on the green image.
# * #4568: the manifest PUT read the whole body before checking credentials.
#   crane's retry reuses the spent request (Content-Length set, 0 bytes
#   written): the body read failed and the client got 500 instead of the 401
#   push challenge.
# * #4578: promotion copied only the tag's `artifacts` row and the manifest
#   object. The target answered MANIFEST_UNKNOWN / NAME_UNKNOWN while the API
#   said `promoted: true`; a source with a missing blob still "promoted".
# * #4558 / #4020: /v2/token drew from the login endpoint's 10-per-15-min
#   per-(username, IP) bucket (#4020, 1.11.0 dev), so an ordinary push + sign +
#   verify got 429; #4558 gave it its own bucket
#   (RATE_LIMIT_TOKEN_EXCHANGE_PER_WINDOW, default 300). 1.10.0 does not limit
#   /v2/token at all, so "twelve good exchanges, then the login still 200" is
#   a CONTROL against 1.10.0 (it was red only on 1.11.0 dev builds). The
#   discriminating half: profiles/limits.token-exchange.yml sets the bucket to
#   20 and the 21st exchange must answer 429 + Retry-After (never on 1.10.0).
#
# PRIMITIVES: raw /v2 wire pushes (no docker daemon), `docker restart` of this
# slot's backend, `psql` against this slot's DB (the source `oci_blobs` row is
# deleted to make an incomplete source image), a python socket for the
# truncated PUT.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED stays ON (the base default): the token-bucket legs need
# the limiter, and the oracle authenticates once as admin and reuses the JWT
# (the API bucket is 10000/min). The token legs run LAST because they exhaust
# the token user's /v2/token bucket.
#
# Red: ak-backend:1.10.0. Green: ak-backend:1.11.0 and main.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem limits.token-exchange"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
